{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>Beyond the Jordan.</b> Opposite the wilderness." "<b>After the way of the going down of the sun.</b> Its meaning is: you shall go after the way westward and find them." "<b>In the land of the Canaanite who dwells in the Arabah.</b> For there is a Canaanite who dwells in the hill country." "<b>Opposite Gilgal.</b> And the mountains are long, and behold, He specified which place among the mountains. <b>Opposite Gilgal</b> — like וירדוף עד דן (Genesis 14:14), or by way of prophecy, or two names." "<b>Opposite.</b> Like נכח." "<b>The oaks of Moreh.</b> It is the one mentioned in the days of Abraham. And the blessing and the curse he will yet explain."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:23:09.627906096Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}